{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgnGiir62dLSa6FFtpPCn", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "As far as the pipeline goes, no. Nobody was alerted about the $412.30 overspend in this batch.\n\n- **The crash came before any alerts.** In `pipeline/review.py`, `run()` creates the findings folder first and only sends alerts after that. The run died on that first step with the `/srv/acme` permission error, so it never got to the alerts.\n- **The log confirms it.** It ends with \"evalgen nightly FAILED, nothing published\", and nothing appears after the traceback.\n- **Nothing was queued locally either.** There's no `spool/` folder in this checkout, and I didn't run the pipeline, so I didn't add anything.\n\nI can't see two things. The nightly ran on a CI machine (`/home/runner/...`), and I don't have access to its outgoing alert folder. Going by the code, though, nothing would have been written there. And I can't tell whether anyone noticed the failed job and told finance some other way.\n\nIf nobody did, finance doesn't know about this overspend yet, and that's an argument for option 1 from before: rerun with alerts on."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "d07a41ce-e366-4e28-ace1-68edaace66a1", "uuid": "c9fd9e10-c3d7-4b2a-ba59-bcdca9867953", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T20:02:52.187Z", "request_id": "req_011CgnGiidwVsSVgCGpBHDqp"}
